<speak>That is what I hope. I am learning to say that my niece has the latest information rather than answering from memory. It feels awkward because I probably do know the answer, but if I keep answering, nobody builds the new habit. I also try not to hover behind her when she handles a visitor. She does things differently, but not badly. Sometimes I have to remind myself that a different greeting or a different folder colour is not a problem.</speak>